finalText:
**Plan ready. Nothing changed.**

The catch: "same data" is not one thing. `buildRows()` in [report.js:11](src/report.js:11) makes 6 fields. `toTable` in [format.js:7](src/format.js:7) prints only 4. It drops `owner` and `slow` on purpose, for width.

JSON has no width limit. So I would print all 6 fields. Say the word if you want the 4.

The change, in [cli.js:8](src/cli.js:8):

```js
function main(argv) {
  const [command, ...flags] = argv;
  if (command !== 'report') { process.stderr.write(USAGE + '\n'); return 1; }
  const rows = buildRows();
  const out = flags.includes('--json') ? JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2) : toTable(rows);
  process.stdout.write(out + '\n');
  return 0;
}
```

`USAGE` gets `[--json]`. No touch to `report.js` or `format.js`.

Next: say go, and pick 6 fields or 4.
